  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "When a draft is submitted",
      "items": [
        "Typing keeps a private draft on this device. Leaving the case, Cmd+Enter or Ctrl+Enter, Escape, or 30 seconds without an edit submits it. Hiding the page also submits it.",
        "A submitted draft is a proposal. Version 1 exists only after acceptance; later accepted content changes add versions. A blank draft or unchanged content adds no version."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Who accepts a proposal",
      "items": [
        "Loose accepts ordinary edits by rule. Standard asks a person to accept or refuse an agent’s edit; a person’s ordinary edit is accepted by rule. Strict asks a person for every ordinary edit, with a reason.",
        "The proposal waits in the queue where a person is required. Refusing it records the answer and leaves the current version alone."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "An older version is a base, not an error",
      "items": [
        "Mainworthy merges compatible changes automatically. Conflicting changes wait for a choice by the author if a person, or a human admin. An agent author may withdraw the proposal and try again on the current version.",
        "A manual merge creates a fresh proposal under the original author’s identity. The policy still applies. More recent overlapping edits can cause another conflict. The device keeps text that the confirmed merge has not recorded."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "History and archive",
      "items": [
        "Restoring old content is a proposal too. Acceptance adds a new version containing that content; the old versions stay. If the content already matches, no new version is needed.",
        "Archiving and bringing a case back also go through a proposal and acceptance under the policy. They change whether the case is active, without adding a content version."
      ]
    }
  ]
